# UI/UX Pro Max — Hospital Portal override

When `ui-ux-pro-max` (or any UI/UX polish / design / layout request) is active, this rule **overrides** generated palettes, fonts, stacks, and visual styles.

Canonical companion docs: `01-design-system`, `02-healthcare-ux`, `10-accessibility`, `00-hospital-architecture`, and `design-system/hospitalportal/MASTER.md`.

## Priority (highest wins)

1. Patient safety / clinical correctness  
2. Privacy / security / permissions  
3. Financial integrity  
4. Backend source of truth  
5. Existing design system + stack freeze  
6. ui-ux-pro-max UX guidelines and pre-delivery checklist  

Never sacrifice (1)–(5) for visual consistency from the skill.

## Allowed uses of ui-ux-pro-max

- Pre-delivery checklist (contrast, focus, keyboard, reduced motion, wrapping chips/badges, truncated labels)
- UX domain searches: empty/error/loading, form validation visibility, resilient text, cancellable interactions
- Density / hierarchy / spacing polish **within** existing layouts
- Stack tips for **Next.js 14 + React 18 + Tailwind 3 + shadcn/ui + Lucide** already in use
- Page-level notes under `design-system/hospitalportal/pages/` (deviations only)

## Forbidden (unless user explicitly approves a redesign)

- New color systems, primary hues, or “Soft UI / Glass / Bento / marketing hero” restyles of staff worklists
- New font families or Google Fonts imports that replace current typography
- New UI frameworks, toast libraries, icon packs (no Phosphor, MUI, Ant, etc.)
- New global token files or a fourth “primary”
- Replacing SignalR, auth, or inventing mock clinical/financial rows to “look complete”
- Merging patient-portal / kiosk patterns into staff desktop workstations

## Tokens and primitives (SoT)

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Staff chrome | Navy sidebar + emerald `primary-*` (`globals.css` / Tailwind) |
| Components | `apps/hospital-portal-web/src/components/ui/*` (shadcn) |
| Icons | Lucide only |
| Toasts | `react-hot-toast` |
| Overlays | Dialog / Sheet / `IpOverlayDialog` — no third overlay stack |
| Scoped themes | Keep `.ip-target`, `.counselling-session`, `.auth-oc`, patient portal — do not unify |

## Workflow prompts (preferred)

- “Review this screen with ui-ux-pro-max checklist; keep navy/emerald and existing domain badges.”
- “Apply resilient chip/badge and focus rules using current components.”
- “Improve empty/error/loading states only.”

## Persisted design system

- Master SoT for agent UX guidance: `design-system/hospitalportal/MASTER.md` (hand-constrained; not raw generator output)
- Page overrides: `design-system/hospitalportal/pages/<page>.md` only for real deviations
- If MASTER and the skill disagree, **MASTER + `.cursor/rules` win**
